INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_entry` (`ID`, `Kind`, `Zone`, `SortOrder`, `Faction`, `RequiredState`, `Title`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(79600, 0, 796, 0, 0, 0, 'Scarlet Monastery', 'The Scarlet Monastery stands in the hills of northeastern Tirisfal, above the gardens where the Scarlet Crusade keeps its watch. Before the plague it was a house of Lordaeron''s priesthood, where the faithful came to study and to seek the Light. After the Scourge overran the kingdom in the Third War, the Crusade made it a fortress, and it is now the order''s great seat in the glades. Its zealots hold that any outsider may carry the plague, and they meet intruders swearing that the Light condemns all who harbor evil. From the vestibule four ways lead in: to the graveyard where prisoners suffer and the dead do not rest, to the library, to the armory and its training halls, and to the cathedral at the monastery''s heart. Scarlet Commander Mograine leads the soldiers of the cathedral, but the monastery''s true master is said to be High Inquisitor Whitemane. The Forsaken want its zealots dead, and scholars far away send for the books on its shelves.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Scarlet_Monastery_(original): northeast corner of Tirisfal Glades; a seminary taken by the Crusade after the Third War; the pre-Cataclysm official description (once a proud bastion of Lordaeron''s priesthood, a center for learning and enlightenment; converted into a stronghold of the Crusade; outsiders seen as potential carriers of the plague; Scarlet Commander Mograine commands a large garrison of fanatically devoted warriors; the true master is High Inquisitor Whitemane, a fearsome priestess); areatrigger_teleport 45, 610, 612, 614 (Graveyard, Cathedral, Armory, Library entrances on map 189) and 602-608 (exits to the Grand Vestibule at 2870-2914,-802 to -822 on map 0); WMOAreaTable 28971-28973 The Grand Vestibule (WMO 60, area 796); creature_text 4283-4303, 4540 (The Light condemns all who harbor evil. Now you will die!; You carry the taint of the Scourge), said on aggro (20 percent) by the Scarlet trash of every wing, base and module (the module gives the same lines to 4280-4285); tirisfal.json 8514 Whispering Gardens (the gardens and the Terrace of Repose up to the doors), pointed to in one clause; quest 1113 (the Forsaken''s Faranell), 1048/14355 (the Undercity''s order), 1050 and 1951 (books sought from Ironforge and Dustwallow) as premises only'),
(79601, 1, 796, 1, 0, 0, 'The Graveyard', 'The Graveyard wing begins in the Chamber of Atonement, and the name is a cruel one. Scarlet torturers work there among wretched undead captives, and their talk is all of confession: confess and be set free, they say, for everyone talks in the end, though one will admit he does not care what is said, since he simply enjoys inflicting pain. Interrogator Vishas keeps his post among them. Beyond lies the Forlorn Cloister, a graveyard where nothing rests. Restless spirits drift between the graves, rotting corpses walk and phantasms haunt the dark, and at the far end stairs lead down into the crypts of Honor''s Tomb.', 'WMOAreaTable 21379 Chamber of Atonement, 21385-21391 Honor''s Tomb, 21392 Forlorn Cloister (WMO 1629, the Graveyard), 3.3.5 DBC: shown as minimap subzone names; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Scarlet_Monastery_(original) lists the same three for the Graveyard; creature 4306 Scarlet Torturer x12 at 1751-1808,1118-1170 next to the entrance (areatrigger 45 lands at 1689,1053); creature 6547 Suffering Victim x2 at 1757,1146 and 1794,1145 among them, display 1027 (ScourgeMale model), faction 68; creature_text 4306 (Confess and we shall set you free; You will talk eventually; What? Oh no, I don''t care what you have to say. I just enjoy inflicting pain): base smart_scripts 4306 say group 0 on aggro (20 percent); module dungeon_scarlet_monastery.sql says group 0 out of combat every 60 to 180 seconds and gives the same lines to the Scarlet Scryers 4293 it pools with the torturers (pools 601001-601007); creature 3983 Interrogator Vishas at 1787,1124 among the torturers; creature 4308 Unfettered Spirit x43 (Ghost model), 6426 Anguished Dead x13 (Zombie models), 6427 Haunting Phantasm x6 (Shade model) at 1739-1854,1244-1434'),
(79602, 1, 796, 2, 0, 0, 'The Library', 'The Library wing holds the Huntsman''s Cloister, the Gallery of Treasures and the Athenaeum. Near the way in, Scarlet gallants and beastmasters keep packs of tracking hounds, and further on, monks, chaplains and diviners stand watch among long tables and reading stands. The books laid out on them are histories of the world: the War of the Ancients, the World Tree and the Emerald Dream, Arathor and the troll wars, and darker chapters, it is said, wait in the farther halls where the library''s keeper walks.', 'WMOAreaTable 21420/21425/21427 Gallery of Treasures, 21426/21435/21438 Athenaeum, 21444 Huntsman''s Cloister (WMO 1631, the Library); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Scarlet_Monastery_(original) lists the same three for the Library; creature spawns on map 189: entrance (areatrigger 614) at 255,-209; Scarlet Gallant 4287 x21 at 154-271,-223 to -313; Beastmaster 4288 x4 and Tracking Hound 4304 x7 at 120-201,-230 to -276; Monk 4540 x17, Chaplain 4299 x8, Diviner 4291 x16 at 174-280,-302 to -445; gameobjects type 9 (readable books) on map 189: 175727 The War of the Ancients, 175730 The World Tree and the Emerald Dream, 175734 Arathor and the Troll Wars (239-275,-306 to -432); 175754 Kel''Thuzad and the Forming of the Scourge (146,-445), 175761 Civil War in the Plaguelands (148,-413), 175749 Icecrown and the Frozen Throne (161,-440), 175756 The Scourge of Lordaeron (219,-424); Arcanist Doan 6487 at 148,-429; chairs 176665-176693 at the tables'),
(79603, 1, 796, 3, 0, 0, 'The Armory', 'The Armory wing is where the Crusade drills and arms its soldiers. Its halls are the Training Grounds, the Footman''s Armory and the Crusader''s Armory, held by soldiers, guardsmen and protectors, evokers, myrmidons and defenders, with crates of armor and weapons among them. At the far end a heavy door opens on the Hall of Champions, where plaques honor the order''s heroes.', 'WMOAreaTable 21448/21449/32248 Hall of Champions, 21455 Footman''s Armory, 21457 Training Grounds, 21460 Crusader''s Armory (WMO 1632, the Armory); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Scarlet_Monastery_(original) lists the same four; creature spawns on map 189 from the entrance (areatrigger 612, 1611,-323): Scarlet Soldier 4286 x17, Conjuror 4297, Guardsman 4290 x7, Protector 4292 x11, Evoker 4289 x4, Myrmidon 4295 x13, Defender 4298 x13 at 1630-1932,-334 to -440; gameobjects 3703 Armor Crate (1772,-377) and 3704 Weapon Crate (1745,-358); gameobject 101854 Herod''s Door at 1934,-432 (lock 299); Herod 3975 at 1965,-432; gameobjects 175771-175781 (type 9 plaques) at 1945-1988,-409 to -455 around Herod, page_text 2151-2178: Orman of Stromgarde, the first Captain General, lost at the mouth of Icecrown Glacier; Admiral Barean Westwind, Grand Admiral of the Scarlet Fleet, lost off the Frozen Coast of Northrend; Ferren Marcus, High Abbot of the Scarlet Monastery, killed defending it at the First Summertide Assault; Fellari Swiftarrow lost in the forests of Silverpine; Dorgar Stoenbrow last seen in the Mountains of Alterac; Valea Twinblades last seen deep in the Eastern Plaguelands; Harthal Truesight last seen entering Stratholme; others (Arellas Fireleaf, Holia Sunshield, Invar One-Arm, Yana Bloodspear)'),
(79604, 1, 796, 4, 0, 0, 'The Cathedral', 'The Cathedral wing is the heart of the monastery. Its way leads through the Chapel Gardens, held by sorcerers, wizards, centurions, myrmidons and defenders, to the doors of the Crusader''s Chapel. Every wing of the monastery keeps its own road, but this one leads to those who command the rest, and its guards are the order''s best. Within the chapel the order''s commanders keep their seats and its abbots, monks and chaplains keep the nave.', 'WMOAreaTable 21401-21417 Crusader''s Chapel, 21410/22063 Chapel Gardens (WMO 1630, the Cathedral); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Scarlet_Monastery_(original) lists the same two; creature spawns on map 189 from the entrance (areatrigger 610, 856,1322): Sorcerer 4294, Myrmidon 4295, Defender 4298 at 865-1046; Wizard 4300 and Centurion 4301 at 909-1141; Chapel Door 104591 at 1070,1399; Abbot 4303, Monk 4540, Champion 4302, Chaplain 4299 at 1079-1167; Mograine 3976 at 1154,1398; gameobject 104600 High Inquisitor''s Door at 1173,1399; Whitemane 3977 at 1202,1399; gameobject 97700 Secret Door at 1168,1347 and 97701 Torch at 1169,1346; smart_scripts 97701 (source_type 1): on state change activate gameobject guid 11876 (the Secret Door); Fairbanks 4542 at 1159,1354; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/High_Inquisitor_Fairbanks (access through a torch on the wall)'),
(79605, 2, 796, 1, 0, 0, 'High Inquisitor Whitemane', 'High Inquisitor Whitemane is a priestess of the Light and, by every account, the true master of the Scarlet Monastery. Scarlet Commander Mograine leads the soldiers of the cathedral, but it is Whitemane who directs the Crusade''s work from within its walls, and she is spoken of as a fearsome woman. She keeps to her own chambers behind the Crusader''s Chapel, beyond the High Inquisitor''s Door at the commander''s back, with a staff in her hand and the chapel between her and any intruder.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Sally_Whitemane (High Inquisitor, priestess of the Light, directed the Crusade''s activities from within the Cathedral); the pre-Cataclysm official description (the monastery''s true master, a fearsome priestess), quoted on warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Scarlet_Monastery_(original); creature 3977 at 1202,1399 behind gameobject 104600 High Inquisitor''s Door (1173,1399); Mograine 3976 at 1154,1398; display 2043 HumanFemale; creature_equip_template 3977 staff 28738'),
(79606, 2, 796, 2, 0, 0, 'Scarlet Commander Mograine', 'Scarlet Commander Mograine leads the warriors of the Scarlet Monastery, a large garrison of fanatically devoted soldiers. He stands at the far end of the Crusader''s Chapel, a tall man with a great two-handed mace, and the abbots, monks and champions who fill the chapel are his to call on. The door at his back leads to the chambers of High Inquisitor Whitemane, and no one reaches her except past him.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Scarlet_Commander_Mograine (Scarlet Commander, leads the Crusade''s forces in the monastery, Crusader''s Chapel); the pre-Cataclysm official description (commands a large garrison of fanatically devoted warriors); creature 3976 at 1154,1398; display 2042 HumanMale at scale 1.2; creature_equip_template 3976 two-handed mace 7706; gameobject 104600 High Inquisitor''s Door at 1173,1399'),
(79607, 2, 796, 3, 0, 0, 'Herod', 'Herod bears the title of the Scarlet Champion, and he keeps to the one hall in the monastery named for such men. He waits at the far end of the Armory wing in the Hall of Champions, beneath the plaques that honor the Crusade''s fallen heroes, a towering man with a great two-handed axe. The soldiers and defenders of the training halls stand between him and the door, and those who make war on the Crusade name him among the monastery''s leaders.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Herod (The Scarlet Champion; Hall of Champions in the Armory); creature_template 3975 subname The Scarlet Champion; creature 3975 at 1965,-432 among plaques 175771-175781; display 2041 HumanMale at scale 1.3; creature_equip_template 3975 two-handed axe 7612'),
(79608, 2, 796, 4, 0, 0, 'Houndmaster Loksey', 'Houndmaster Loksey keeps the Crusade''s hounds in the Library wing, not far from the way in. Tracking hounds lie close about him, and the Scarlet beastmasters nearby keep more of them, for the Crusade uses such dogs to hunt down its enemies. He carries an axe in each hand and does not stray from his pack. Whoever means to reach the books and the arcanist beyond must first get past the houndmaster and his dogs.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Houndmaster_Loksey (the captain in charge of training the hounds the Crusade used to track down its enemies); creature 3974 at 120,-261 with Scarlet Tracking Hounds 4304 at 121-124,-258 to -261 beside him, more hounds and Beastmasters 4288 at 167-201,-230 to -276; Library entrance at 255,-209 (areatrigger 614); Doan 6487 at 148,-429; creature_equip_template 3974 two one-handed axes 5286'),
(79609, 2, 796, 5, 0, 0, 'Arcanist Doan', 'Arcanist Doan is the keeper of the monastery''s library, a mage of the Scarlet Crusade among its priests and warriors. He walks the farthest hall of the Library wing, staff in hand, along the reading stands where the histories of the Scourge lie open, and a strongbox stands close by his path. Monks and chaplains keep watch around him, but the books, and whatever the order guards among them, are his charge.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Arcanist_Doan (human mage of the Crusade; keeper of the Scarlet Monastery''s library); creature 6487 at 148,-429, MovementType 2 (walks a path); books 175754, 175761, 175749 at 146-161,-413 to -445; gameobject 103821 Doan''s Strongbox at 132,-433 (lock 43); Monk 4540 and Chaplain 4299 spawns around; creature_equip_template 6487 staff 2177; display 5266 HumanMale'),
(79610, 2, 796, 6, 0, 0, 'High Inquisitor Fairbanks', 'Off the Crusader''s Chapel, behind a secret door that a torch upon the wall opens, lies a hidden room, and in it waits High Inquisitor Fairbanks. He bears the same title as the monastery''s mistress, yet he has no place among the zealots of the chapel and keeps no door they pass through. Whoever finds him will find him ready, a hammer in his hand. What he once was, and why he lingers in that hidden place, the chapel does not say.', 'creature 4542 at 1159,1354 z30, behind gameobject 97700 Secret Door (1168,1347) opened by 97701 Torch (smart_scripts 97701 activates guid 11876); creature_template 4542 type 6 (undead), faction 67 (the Scarlet Crusade''s, as for every Scarlet creature on map 189); display 2605 ScourgeMale model; creature_equip_template 4542 hammer 2182; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/High_Inquisitor_Fairbanks (in Classic and Wrath an undead hidden in a secret chamber in the Cathedral; access through a torch on the wall)'),
(79611, 3, 796, 1, 1, 0, 'Down the Scarlet Path', 'Brother Anton of Nijel''s Point has a reward for those who prove themselves against the undead of Desolace: a place in the Scarlet Crusade''s work in Lordaeron. He speaks proudly of what his order holds there, a chain of strongholds running from Hearthglen to Tirisfal Glades, each a bastion where the land is cleansed. To the worthy he gives a letter of commendation sealed with his own mark, and sends them across the sea to the town of Southshore. There a crusader called Raleigh the Devout is to receive the letter and take its bearer to the Scarlet Monastery, where Anton promises them a place of honor.', 'quest 1052 description (strongholds from Hearthglen to Tirisfal Glades; bastions of cleansing throughout Lordaeron; proven against the undead in Desolace; the true threat of the plague lies in Lordaeron; Raleigh the Devout in Southshore; letter of commendation bearing my seal; escort you to a place of honor in our Scarlet Monastery); objectives (take Brother Anton''s Letter of Commendation to Raleigh); item 5539 Letter of Commendation (sealed by Brother Anton of the Scarlet Crusade); quest_template 1052: AllowableRaces 1101, QuestType 2, Flags 0, QuestSortID 405 (Desolace), PrevQuestID 261; creature_queststarter 1182 Brother Anton; desolace.json 40526 Brother Anton (TALK 1182), pointed to in the first clause'),
(79612, 3, 796, 2, 2, 0, 'Into the Scarlet Monastery', 'For the Forsaken, the Scarlet Crusade is a war fought on their own doorstep. Its zealots swarm over Tirisfal, hunting the dead wherever they walk, and their stronghold, the Scarlet Monastery, rises in the northeast of the glades. From the Royal Quarter of the Undercity an order goes out to strike at the root: go to the Monastery and kill High Inquisitor Whitemane, along with those who serve directly beneath her, Scarlet Commander Mograine, Herod the Scarlet Champion, and Houndmaster Loksey with his hounds.', 'quest 1048 and 14355 descriptions and objectives (both: kill High Inquisitor Whitemane, Scarlet Commander Mograine, Herod, the Scarlet Champion and Houndmaster Loksey); 1048: Tirisfal literally crawling with the little red ants; 14355: the Crusade a problem on the Forsaken''s borders; both AllowableRaces 690, QuestType 2 (1048 Flags 16392: 8 plus 0x4000 QUEST_FLAGS_UNAVAILABLE, which no core code reads; 14355 Flags 8); base world database: creature_queststarter/questender 2425 for 1048, but Varimathras 2425 has no creature spawn, so 1048 cannot be taken without the module; Bragor 36273 spawned (guid 31901, phaseMask 1) starts and ends 14355; mod-individual-progression zone_undercity.sql: removes 1048 from disables (it is not disabled in the base data); spawns Varimathras 2425 (guid 602425) in the Royal Quarter at phaseMask IPPPHASE_II and moves Bragor (31901) to IPPPHASE_III; adds 2425 and 36273 as enders of 14355 (no new starter for either quest); rewrites 14355''s log text to Varimathras and its description to the same Bragor text; IndividualProgression.cpp AREA_UNDERCITY: phase III once the Battle for the Undercity (Horde or Alliance) is rewarded, phase II before'),
(79613, 3, 796, 3, 2, 0, 'Hearts of Zeal', 'In the Apothecarium, Master Apothecary Faranell has plans for the Kraul guano he sent for. He means to set two utterly opposed substances against each other, binding both with a lasting poison, and he expects results of the most horrific kind. The second substance must come from the Scarlet Crusade, whose fanatics crowd the Scarlet Monastery high in the northeast of Tirisfal Glades, in its halls and on its grounds alike. Any one of them may carry what he needs, so it makes no difference which of them fall. He wants twenty Hearts of Zeal.', 'quest 1113 description (two diametrically opposed chemical substances combined with an ever-toxic agent; the most ghastly results; the Scarlet Monastery in the northeastern peaks of Tirisfal Glades; the crazed disciples congregate both inside and outside the halls; which you slay matters not) and objectives (20 Hearts of Zeal); AllowableRaces 690, QuestType 2, Flags 8, PrevQuestID 1109; creature_queststarter/questender 2055 Master Apothecary Faranell (base, guid 31900; the module puts him in phase III) and, with the module, 102055 (phase II, zone_undercity.sql creature_queststarter list includes 1113), so the quest is reachable in every state; razorfen_kraul.json 49102 (quest 1109, the guano), undercity.json 149705 Faranell, pointed to in a phrase'),
(79614, 3, 796, 4, 1, 0, 'Mythology of the Titans', 'In the Hall of Explorers in Ironforge, Librarian Mae Paledust of the Explorers'' League believes no one can escape what is to come, but that those who know the past can face it better prepared. Before Lordaeron''s troubles, she says, a great house of learning lay tucked away in Tirisfal Glades, and rumor holds that its library, in the old Monastery, kept a book called Mythology of the Titans. She wants it found and brought to her, so that together they may uncover the secrets of ages gone.', 'quest 1050 description (the future is inevitable; by studying the past we can know what to expect; before dire troubles fell upon Lordaeron, a bastion of knowledge tucked away in Tirisfal Glades; Mythology of the Titans rumored housed in the library of the old Monastery; together unlock the secrets of the past) and objectives (bring it to Librarian Mae Paledust in Ironforge); AllowableRaces 1101, QuestType 2, Flags 8; creature 3979 Librarian Mae Paledust (Explorers'' League), map 0 area 1537 Ironforge; quest_template 1050 completion log (the Hall of Explorers in Ironforge)');
INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_part` (`Entry`, `Part`, `MinState`, `MaxState`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(79601, 1, 0, 255, 'Below the stairs at the graveyard''s far end, Bloodmage Thalnos rose to meet intruders, a skeletal mage who cried that the dead hunger for vengeance. He hurled bolts of shadow, called down pillars of flame, seared his foes with fire and burst outward in a ring of flame. Wounded, he cried that there is no rest for the angry dead. But the bloodmage fell at last, among the dead he spoke for.', 'creature 4543 Bloodmage Thalnos, single spawn, map 189 only, at 1820,1417 z -8 (below the graveyard, whose spawns run at z 7 to 18); type 6 undead, display 11396 SkeletonMage model at scale 1.3; creature_text 4543 (We hunger for vengeance. on aggro; No rest... for the angry dead! at 40 percent), base and module smart_scripts 4543; smart_scripts 4543 base and module: Shadow Bolt 9613, Flame Spike 8814 (a pillar of flame on an area), Flame Shock 8053, Fire Nova 12470 (Spell.dbc); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Bloodmage_Thalnos (skeletal, just below the staircase at the far end of the graveyard)'),
(79602, 1, 0, 255, 'One book on these shelves came by a strange road. Rituals of Power was written by the Magus Tirth, once a great mage and scholar, who has traded his studies for ale and wagers at the races of the Shimmering Flats. Gambling debts drove him to sell the last copy to one of the Scarlet clergy, and he has no doubt it ended up in the monastery''s library.', 'quest 1951 description (gambling debts; sold the last copy of Rituals of Power to a member of the Scarlet Brotherhood''s clergy; taken to their library in the Scarlet Monastery); quest 1949 description (Tirth used to be a great mage and scholar, now drinking and gambling at the races in the Shimmering Flats), the step before it; quest_template 1951: AllowableClasses 128 (mage), QuestType 2, Flags 8; started by 6548 Magus Tirth (map 1, Shimmering Flats); item 7274 Rituals of Power (By Magus Tirth) from gameobject 103664, single spawn on map 189 at 278,-429 in the library'),
(79605, 1, 0, 255, 'When Mograine fell, the door behind him swung open and Whitemane came out crying that Mograine had fallen, that the intruders would pay for this treachery. She smote her foes with holy fire and shielded those beside her, until she cast a deep sleep over everyone near her and went to the fallen commander. Arise, my champion, she called, and he rose. Then she fought at his side, healing him and bending her foes'' minds to her will, until at last she fell.', 'creature 3977, single spawn, map 189 only; creature_text 3977 (Mograine has fallen! You shall pay for this treachery! Arise, my champion! Arise!; Arise, my champion!); smart_scripts 3977 (base, untouched by the module): on data set by Mograine at 1 percent health, open the High Inquisitor''s Door (guid 11877), yell, move to Mograine; Holy Smite 9481, Power Word: Shield 22187 on friends; invincible at 1 HP until the resurrection; at 50 percent action list 397700 (Deep Sleep 9256: puts nearby enemies to sleep), then 397701 (Scarlet Resurrection 9232 on Mograine, Arise, my champion!); phase 2 Dominate Mind 14515 and Heal 12039 on friends below 75 percent; smart_scripts 3976 event 18 (base and module): on Scarlet Resurrection he stands and goes to her'),
(79606, 1, 0, 255, 'Mograine met intruders crying that the infidels must be purified, and the whole chapel rose to fight beside him. He struck with crusading blows, stunned foes with the hammer of justice, and his aura burned all who struck him. Beaten down, he fell as if dead. Whitemane came for him, and at her call he rose again, crying At your side, milady, and laid healing hands upon her. He fought on until he fell a second time, and this time he did not rise.', 'creature 3976, single spawn, map 189 only; creature_text 3976 (Infidels! They must be purified! on aggro; At your side, milady! when raised); smart_scripts 3976 base and module: Retribution Aura 8990, Crusader Strike 14518, Hammer of Justice 5589; invincible at 1 HP; at 1 percent action list 397600 (lies as dead, unselectable, calls Whitemane); on Scarlet Resurrection 9232 action list 397601 (stands, Lay on Hands 9257 on Whitemane guid 39946, says line 2, goes to her); invincibility reset when he reaches her, so he can die only after the raising; instance_scarlet_monastery.cpp SetData TYPE_MOGRAINE_AND_WHITE_EVENT IN_PROGRESS (set by Mograine on combat): Scarlet Monks, Abbots, Champions, Centurions, Wizards and Chaplains within 80 yards attack his target'),
(79607, 1, 0, 255, 'Herod met intruders glad of a real challenge at last. He cleaved through those beside him and spun into a whirlwind of steel, crying Blades of light. Badly wounded, he called on the Light to give him strength and flew into a rage. Yet the Scarlet Champion fell. As he died, a crowd of Scarlet trainees poured into the hall, crying that the master had fallen and calling on their brethren to avenge him.', 'creature 3975, single spawn, map 189 only; creature_text 3975 (Ah - I''ve been waiting for a real challenge!; Blades of light!; Light, give me strength!; becomes enraged!) and 6575 (The master has fallen! Avenge him, my brethren!); smart_scripts 3975 (base, untouched by the module): Cleave 15496, Whirlwind 8989 with Blades of light every 15 seconds, Frenzy 8269 with the enrage emote and Light, give me strength! at 50 percent health; on death summon creature group 1 (creature_summon_groups 3975: twenty Scarlet Trainees 6575 at 1920-1928,-418 to -440, inside the hall) and the nearest says its line; smart_scripts 6575: set in combat with the zone'),
(79608, 1, 0, 255, 'Loksey met intruders with a cry of Release the hounds, and the tracking hounds around him leapt to the attack. He drove them on with a battle fury that quickened their bites while he cut at his foes with his two axes. Neither the dogs nor their master could hold, and the houndmaster fell among his pack.', 'creature 3974, single spawn, map 189 only; creature_text 3974 (Release the hounds!) on aggro; smart_scripts 3974 (base, untouched by the module): Bloodlust 6742 (Spell.dbc: increases an ally''s attack speed) cast on Scarlet Tracking Hounds 4304 within 20 yards'),
(79609, 1, 0, 255, 'Doan met intruders crying that they would not defile these mysteries. He loosed blasts of arcane power, silenced those who would cast spells and turned his foes into sheep. Wounded, he wrapped himself in a bubble of arcane force, then let it burst in a detonation, crying Burn in righteous fire. It did not save him, and the keeper of the library fell among his books.', 'creature 6487, single spawn, map 189 only; creature_text 6487 (You will not defile these mysteries! on aggro; Burn in righteous fire! at 50 percent); smart_scripts 6487 (base, untouched by the module): Arcane Explosion 9433, Silence 8988, Polymorph 13323, at 50 percent Arcane Bubble 9438 (immune to all attacks and spells) then Detonation 9435 and the line'),
(79610, 1, 0, 255, 'Those who opened the hidden room found what it kept from the chapel: Fairbanks is undead, one of the very dead the Crusade has sworn to destroy, yet he fought for the Crusade still. He fought with a priest''s magic, laying a curse of blood on his foes that made every blow against them bite deeper, stripping away the magic that guarded them, wrapping himself in a shield of light and healing his own wounds. None of it was enough, and the undead inquisitor fell in his hidden room.', 'creature 4542, single spawn, map 189 only; smart_scripts 4542 (base, untouched by the module): Curse of Blood 8282 (increases physical damage taken), Dispel Magic 15090, Power Word: Shield 11647 and Heal 12039 on himself (Spell.dbc)'),
(79611, 1, 0, 255, 'In Southshore, Raleigh the Devout met the letter''s bearer with suspicion, demanding to know who had come and what they wanted of him. Anton''s seal brought no welcome. Raleigh seemed only dismayed to learn that the brother was still out preaching for the Scarlet Crusade.', 'quest 1052 request text (Who goes there? What do you want from me?) and reward text (Brother Anton still spreads the word of the Scarlet Crusade? Oh my....); creature_questender 3980 Raleigh the Devout (map 0, area 271 Southshore)'),
(79611, 2, 0, 255, 'Raleigh had once been one of them. He served the Crusade faithfully and proudly, sure that ridding Azeroth of the undead was a noble cause. Time at the Monastery changed his mind: he watched its zealots lose their hold on reality, until anyone without the Crusade''s tabard counted as plagued, and innocent men and women were tortured for it. Now he wants the order crushed in the Light''s name, starting at the top: Whitemane, Mograine, Herod and Loksey.', 'quest 1053 description (served the Scarlet Crusade with honor, loyalty and pride; a noble cause, to rid Azeroth of the undead; at the Monastery their grasp on reality was slipping; everyone who doesn''t wear the tabard thought plagued; innocent men and women tortured; crushed in the name of the Light) and objectives (High Inquisitor Whitemane, Scarlet Commander Mograine, Herod, Houndmaster Loksey); AllowableRaces 1101, QuestType 2, Flags 8, PrevQuestID 1052'),
(79611, 3, 0, 255, 'Raleigh believed the rot in the Monastery would last as long as its highest officers did, and that only with them gone could the cause he once served be kindled anew. When word came that the four had fallen he did not rejoice, for a servant of the Light takes no pleasure in killing. Still, he held that such sacrifices are sometimes the price of the greater good, for the kingdom and for the world, and that many innocents would live because of what was done in the Monastery.', 'quest 1053 request text (the corruption will not end until the highest ranking officials have been removed; perhaps the true cause can be rekindled) and reward text (disciples of the Light never revel in the loss of life; such sacrifices for the greater good of the Kingdom and the planet; spared many innocent lives); creature_questender 3980'),
(79612, 1, 0, 255, 'The order came from the dreadlord Varimathras. With the Dark Lady occupied by the Lich King''s advance in the north, he had taken it upon himself to set the homeland in order, and no trouble at home galled him more than the human vermin of the Scarlet Crusade, whose red-clad zealots infest the glades. He wanted Whitemane and her chief lieutenants destroyed.', 'quest 1048 description (whilst the Dark Lady tends to the pressing issue of the Lich King''s advance to the north; matters closer to home; the human pests who call themselves the Scarlet Crusade, the sharpest thorn in our side domestically; Tirisfal crawling with the little red ants; lay waste to High Inquisitor Whitemane and her top lieutenants); creature_queststarter 2425 Varimathras'),
(79612, 2, 0, 255, 'Varimathras would settle for nothing short of Whitemane dead for good, and her commanders with her: the zealot Mograine, the champion Herod, and Loksey along with his dogs. When the deed was done, he conceded that it had been no easy errand. The Dark Lady had been served well, he declared; such loyalty to the Forsaken would not go unnoticed, nor would such stubbornness in battle be forgotten.', 'quest 1048 request text (Whitemane killed once and for all; her top brass; that zealot Mograine; Herod; Loksey and his filthy mutts) and reward text (served the Dark Lady well; no small task; loyalty to the Forsaken noted; tenacity in combat remembered); creature_questender 2425'),
(79612, 3, 13, 255, 'In the Royal Quarter, the order was given by Bragor Bloodfist, an orc who counts helping the Forsaken guard their borders among his duties in the Undercity. His reasons were his own as well as theirs: he lives and breathes, yet the Crusade would slay his kind as readily as any of the undead. With Whitemane and her lieutenants slain, he was sure Sylvanas would welcome the news. It had been a hard task, he granted, and a victory like that earns respect.', 'quest 14355 description (one of my duties while I''m stationed here is to help the Forsaken take care of their borders; I might live and breathe, but the Scarlet Crusade will cut down my people as quickly as one of the undead; a big problem; slay Whitemane and her lieutenants) and reward text (Sylvanas will be glad to have that problem taken care of; the task wasn''t easy; victorious; commands respect, won''t be forgotten); creature_queststarter/questender 36273 Bragor Bloodfist; undercity.json 149706 Bragor Bloodfist (requiredState 13; ACCEPT 14355 is its trigger and 149707''s, not used here)'),
(79613, 1, 0, 255, 'Faranell had waited eagerly for the hearts, for his delightful experiment would need a great many. When twenty Hearts of Zeal, cut from the Crusade''s zealots, were set before him, he was overjoyed at so generous a heap of gore and praised the labor that had gathered it.', 'quest 1113 request text (I''ll need many hearts for this delightful experiment) and reward text (what an abundance of gore you have brought me; your efforts have been most excellent); item 5805 Heart of Zeal: creature_loot_template (quest-only) of every Scarlet creature of the Monastery and its gardens (4280-4306, 4540) and of its leaders'),
(79614, 1, 0, 255, 'Mae Paledust knew the old Monastery''s story. Paladins once trained there, and it stood as a stronghold of the Light until the fanatics of the Scarlet Crusade took it. They thought their purpose noble, to cleanse the land of the undead plague, but madness crept into the cause, and now they are the enemies of everyone. Halls so corrupted were no fit home for so precious a record of the past. With the book recovered, she gave thanks on behalf of the League.', 'quest 1050 request text (the Monastery was a seminary for Paladins-in-training; once a stronghold of the Light; fell into the hands of the crazed zealots of the Scarlet Crusade; a noble goal, to purify the land of the undead plague; insanity tainted their plight; enemies to all; the corrupt halls no place for such a historical treasure) and reward text (rescued the sacred text; thank you on behalf of the Explorers'' League)'),
(79614, 2, 0, 255, 'The book begins where all things began. No one knows how the universe was born, it says, but a race of powerful beings arose to bring it order: the titans, colossal gods with skin of metal, who raised mountains, dredged seas and breathed skies into being. Ruled by the Pantheon, they ordered a hundred million worlds, ever watchful against the demons of the Twisting Nether.', 'item 5536 Mythology of the Titans, PageText 575-578 (no one knows exactly how the universe began; the Titans, colossal, metallic-skinned gods; raised mountains, dredged seas, breathed skies into being; ruled by the Pantheon; a hundred million worlds; vigilant against the demonic beings of the Twisting Nether); looted from gameobject 19284, single spawn on map 189 at 281,-352 in the library');
